reference.api:
```
POST /v1/blocks/missing  {hashes[]}                  → {missing[]}
PUT  /v1/blocks/{sha256}  (bytes, ≤4 MB)             → 201
POST /v1/files/commit    {namespace, path, manifest[], parent_rev} → 200 {rev} | 409 conflict
POST /v1/sync/list_delta {namespace, cursor}         → {changes[], cursor}
WS   /v1/sync/listen     → server pushes {namespace, latest_seq}
GET  /v1/blocks/{sha256}                             → bytes (CDN-cacheable)
```
- Upload asks which blocks are missing, sends only those, then commits a manifest.
- The push channel carries a cursor, never file bytes; the client then pulls the delta.
